content:
{
  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "Sample size calculation inconsistent: 9 cohorts × 25 subjects = 225, but Table 12 lists 9 cohorts with ORR values, yet the text says 'approximately 225' which is correct, but the table has an error for cohort F: lower bound of 90% CI is listed as '>21%' while the observed ORR is 40% and the ORR of available treatment is 19% – the lower bound should be compared to 19%, not 21%.",
      "page": 91,
      "quote": "F  19%  40%  >21%",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Safety Analysis Set is defined as primary for efficacy, but efficacy endpoints are analyzed per cohort; however, the primary efficacy endpoint (confirmed ORR) is defined as proportion in Safety Analysis Set, which is appropriate, but the text says 'primary analysis set for all efficacy and safety endpoints' – this is not an error per se, but the issue is that the Safety Analysis Set includes subjects who receive at least 1 dose of study drug, which is standard. No error found here.",
      "page": 91,
      "quote": "The Safety Analysis Set is defined as all subjects who receive at least 1 dose of study drug. This analysis set will be the primary analysis set for all efficacy and safety endpoints.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent reporting of SAE collection period: Section 7.3.1 says AEs recorded from informed consent until 100 days after last dose, but Section 7.3.2 says SAEs collected from completion of ICF until 100 days after last dose – 'completion of ICF' is ambiguous but likely same. However, Section 7.3.2 also says 'SAEs will be collected from completion of the ICF until 100 days after the last dose of any study allowed drug treatment' – this is consistent. No error.",
      "page": 87,
      "quote": "SAEs will be collected from completion of the ICF until 100 days after the last dose of any study allowed drug treatment.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Pregnancy reporting window inconsistency: Section 7.3.3 says female subjects or partners of male subjects who become pregnant within 150 days of last vidutolimod dose will be instructed to notify, but then says 'If the Investigator learns of a report of pregnancy at any time after the W1D1 visit up to 150 days after the last dose of the study drug' – the first part says 'within 150 days of their last vidutolimod dose' but the second says 'up to 150 days after the last dose of the study drug' – 'study drug' could mean both, but it's ambiguous. Also, the first part says 'within 150 days of their last vidutolimod dose' which is a window, but the second says 'up to 150 days after' which is a deadline. This is a minor inconsistency.",
      "page": 88,
      "quote": "Female subjects or the partners of male subjects who become pregnant within 150 days of their last vidutolimod dose will be instructed to notify the Investigator immediately. If the Investigator learns of a report of pregnancy at any time after the W1D1 visit up to 150 days after the last dose of the study drug",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Cross-reference to Section 4.1.1.4 and 4.1.2.2 for dose modifications, but these sections are not provided in the excerpt; cannot verify existence, but it's a potential missing cross-reference.",
      "page": 86,
      "quote": "Refer to Section 4.1.1.4 and Section 4.1.2.2 for vidutolimod and cemiplimab allowed dose modifications.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "In Section 7.3.2, it says 'All SAEs and associated source documents must be reported ... within 24 hours of first knowledge' but later says 'A paper SAE Report Form should be completed and submitted within 24 hours of awareness.' This is consistent. No error.",
      "page": 87,
      "quote": "All SAEs and associated source documents must be reported in written or typed English via completion of the eCRF AE page and accompanying paper SAE Report Form (following the same reporting process outlined in Section 7.3) within 24 hours of first knowledge of the event",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "In Section 7.3.4, AESI list includes 'Grade ≥2 Allergic /hypersensitivity reactions (cemiplimab and/or vidutolimod)' and 'Grade ≥2 Injection site reactions (vidutolimod)' – but later in the same list, 'Grade ≥2 cytokine release syndrome (CRS, vidutolimod): Hypotension responding to fluids, and/or hypoxia responding to <40% O2.' – This is not an error.",
      "page": 89,
      "quote": "Grade ≥2 Allergic /hypersensitivity reactions (cemiplimab and/or vidutolimod)",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "In Section 8.1, Table 12 lists ORR of available treatment for Cohort F as 19%, but the lower bound of 90% CI is listed as '>21%' – this is inconsistent because the lower bound should be compared to the ORR of available treatment (19%), not 21%. This is a numerical error.",
      "page": 91,
      "quote": "F  19%  40%  >21%",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "In Section 8.6.1, the primary efficacy endpoint is confirmed ORR based on RECIST v1.1 as determined by the Investigator, but the analysis set is Safety Analysis Set, which is defined as all subjects who receive at least 1 dose of study drug. This is standard, but the protocol does not specify how subjects without post-baseline tumor assessment are handled beyond those who discontinue due to death or progression – it says 'Subjects who discontinue prior to having a post-baseline scan for other reasons will be counted as non-responders.' This is fine.",
      "page": 93,
      "quote": "Subjects who discontinue prior to having a post-baseline scan for other reasons will be counted as non-responders.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "In Section 8.6.2, DOR is defined for responders, but the censoring details are deferred to SAP. This is acceptable.",
      "page": 94,
      "quote": "Censoring details will be described in the SAP",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "In Section 8.7.1, it says 'A subject with 2 or more TEAEs within the same level of summarization (i.e. system organ class [SOC] or preferred term) will be counted only once in that level using the most severe event or most related (for the relationship to study treatment tables).' This is fine.",
      "page": 94,
      "quote": "A subject with 2 or more TEAEs within the same level of summarization (i.e. system organ class [SOC] or preferred term) will be counted only once in that level using the most severe event or most related (for the relationship to study treatment tables).",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "In Section 8.8, pharmacodynamic analyses mention CXCL10 and other biomarkers, but no specific analysis methods are described. This is not an error.",
      "page": 95,
      "quote": "Concentrations of peripheral biomarkers including CXCL10 and other chemokine or cytokine biomarkers will be summarized using descriptive statistics for all time points for the Pharmacodynamic Analysis Set.",
      "severity": "minor"
    }
  ]
}
